      command: `# postmortem/2025-05-30_churn_model_v4_incident.md\n\`\`\`markdown\n# Post-Mortem: Churn Model v4 Prediction Degradation\n\n## Incident Summary\n- Date: 2025-05-30\n- Duration: 14:30 - 14:45 UTC (15 minutes)\n- Severity: S1\n- Impact: 5% of predictions returned NaN, affecting premium user retention offers\n\n## Timeline\n| Time | Event |\n|------|-------|\n| 14:30 | Monitoring alert: error rate 5% (threshold: 1%) |\n| 14:31 | Engineer paged, acknowledges |\n| 14:32 | Runs rollback script: ChurnPredictor v4 -> v3 |\n| 14:33 | K8s rolling update starts |\n| 14:35 | Rollback complete, error rate dropping |\n| 14:40 | Error rate back to 0.1% |\n| 14:45 | Incident resolved |\n| 15:00 | Root cause identified: feature_12 null in training data v2025-05-29 |\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n- Training data v2025-05-29 had corrupted feature_12 (all nulls) due to upstream pipeline bug\n- Model v4 trained on corrupted data learned to handle nulls but served different distribution\n- Guardrails caught nulls but fallback value was wrong\n\n## What Went Well\n- Monitoring alert detected immediately (error rate spike)\n- Rollback script worked in 3 minutes\n- Team communicated via Slack incident channel\n\n## What Needs Improvement\n- Guardrail fallback value for feature_12 was incorrect\n- No integration test for feature pipeline output\n- Post-mortem not automated\n\n## Action Items\n| Action | Owner | Due |\n|--------|-------|-----|\n| Fix feature_12 null handling in feature pipeline | DataEng | 2025-06-02 |\n| Add integration test for feature pipeline schema | MLEng | 2025-06-04 |\n| Improve guardrail fallback values per feature | MLEng | 2025-06-05 |\n| Automate post-mortem generation from incident data | Platform | 2025-06-10 |\n| Add feature-level drift monitoring for critical features | MLEng | 2025-06-07 |\n\`\`\``,
        output: "Post-Mortem: Churn Model v4 Prediction Degradation\nSeverity: S1 | Duration: 15 minutes | Impact: 5% NaN predictions\n\nRoot Cause: feature_12 null in training data v2025-05-29\n\nAction Items:\n1. Fix feature pipeline null handling (DataEng, 2025-06-02)\n2. Add integration test for feature schema (MLEng, 2025-06-04)\n3. Improve guardrail fallback values (MLEng, 2025-06-05)\n4. Automate post-mortem generation (Platform, 2025-06-10)\n5. Feature-level drift monitoring for critical features (MLEng, 2025-06-07)",
          explanation: "Post-mortem documents: timeline, root cause, what went well, what needs improvement, action items. Blameless: focus on process improvements, not individual blame.",
            productionMeaning: "Post-mortem is how ML systems improve. Every incident -> action items -> prevention. Blameless culture encourages reporting without fear. Automation reduces manual work."
